│                                                                 │
│  ┌─────────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐              │
│  │  🇬🇧 Voice Language   │  │  Voice to Speak      │              │
│  │  [English (US)    ▾] │  │  [en-US-Standard-A ▾] │              │
│  └─────────────────────┘  └─────────────────────┘              │
│                                                                 │
│  [▶ Preview AI Voice]                                           │
│                                                                 │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐            │
│  │  🔊 Audio Preview Player                        │            │
│  │  ────●─────────────────── 0:03 / 0:05           │            │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘            │
│                                                                 │
│  Comparison:                                                    │
│  ┌──────────────────────┐  ┌──────────────────────┐            │
│  │  Browser Voice (Free) │  │  AI Voice (Pro) ✓    │            │
│  │  [▶ Preview]          │  │  [▶ Preview]          │            │
│  │  Varies by device     │  │  Consistent quality   │            │
│  │  No MP3 files         │  │  Generates MP3        │            │
│  └──────────────────────┘  └──────────────────────┘            │
│                                                                 │
│                    [← Back]  [Next: Player Settings →]          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Provider-specific preview rendering (auto-switches when player is selected in Step 2):**

The preview UI adapts per provider — reference patterns from `Listening.js` (voice selection + audio player) and `Customize.js` (live player demo). Remove multilingual-specific code when adapting.

| Player Selected | Preview Component | UI Elements |
|----------------|-------------------|-------------|
| Player 2 (Pro Player) | `TextToSpeech` | Language + Voice dropdowns (browser voices via `speechSynthesis`) |
| Player 3 (AtlasVoice GTTS) | `TextToSpeechThree` | Language dropdown only (no voice selector). Live demo area with demo text + play button (pattern from `Customize.js`) |
| Player 4 (Google Cloud TTS) | `TextToSpeechFour` | Language + Voice dropdowns + HTML5 audio player. Preview URLs: `https://cloud.google.com/text-to-speech/docs/audio/{voice}.wav` |
| Player 5 (ChatGPT TTS) | `TextToSpeechThree` | Language + Voice (6: alloy/echo/fable/onyx/nova/shimmer) + Model (tts-1/tts-1-hd). Preview URLs: `https://cdn.openai.com/API/docs/audio/{voice}.wav` |
| Player 6 (ElevenLabs) | `TextToSpeechThree` | Language + Voice (with accent) + Model. Preview via `preview_url` from ElevenLabs API voice object |

**Key behavior:** When user selects a player in Step 2 and arrives at Step 3, the correct preview UI is already loaded. Selecting a voice auto-plays the preview audio (same pattern as `Listening.js` `handleChange()`).

**Settings written directly to `tta_listening_settings`** (same option the Listening tab uses — no new options):
- `tta_listening_settings.tta__listening_lang` → selected language
- `tta_listening_settings.tta__listening_voice` → selected voice
- `tta_listening_settings.tta__listening_voice_model` → model (ChatGPT: "tts-1"/"tts-1-hd")
- `tta_listening_settings.tta__elevenlabs_model` → model (ElevenLabs: "eleven_multilingual_v2" etc.)

**Saved via:** `POST /tta/v1/listening` with FormData `{ fields: JSON.stringify(listeningSettings), method: "post" }` — the exact same endpoint and format `Listening.js` uses.

