## Technical Architecture

### File Structure

**Pro plugin** (`text-to-audio-pro/`):
```
text-to-audio-pro/
  src/
    pro-wizard/
      index.js                        ← NEW: Entry point (webpack bundle)
      ProWelcomeWizard.js             ← NEW: Pro wizard container
      wizardApi.js                    ← NEW: REST API helper
      steps/
        StepProPostType.js            ← NEW: Multi-select post types
        StepProvider.js               ← NEW: AI provider selection
        StepProVoice.js               ← NEW: Voice & language for AI provider
        StepPlayerSettings.js         ← NEW: Date range + download permissions
        StepProAnalytics.js           ← NEW: Analytics + email digest
        StepProFinish.js              ← NEW: Pro finish screen
```

**Free plugin** (`text-to-audio/`) — minimal changes:
```
src/dashboard/
  welcome.js                          ← Existing, add: if is_pro_wizard → render Pro wizard root div
```

### Data Flow

```
Free plugin: welcome.js
  └─ if (is_pro_wizard) → render <div id="pro-wizard-root"> (Pro JS takes over)
  └─ else               → <WelcomeWizard />  (existing free wizard)

Pro plugin: pro-wizard/index.js  (separate bundle, enqueued by Pro)
  └─ <ProWelcomeWizard />
        ├─ Reads existing settings from ttsProWizardData (localized by PHP)
        ├─ Step 1: StepProPostType → POST /tta/v1/settings → tta_settings_data
        ├─ Step 2: StepProvider → POST /tta/v1/customize → tta_customize_settings.buttonSettings.id (if production=yes)
        ├─ Step 3: StepProVoice → POST /tta/v1/listening → tta_listening_settings (lang, voice, model)
        ├─ Step 4: StepPlayerSettings → POST /tta/v1/customize → tta_customize_settings (date range, download perms)
        ├─ Step 5: StepProAnalytics → analytics endpoint + POST /tta/v1/save_schedule_report
        └─ Step 6: StepProFinish → summary + actions + cross-promo
```

### API Calls (triggered on "Finish Setup" click — Step 5 → Step 6 transition)

All calls fire **before** the Finish screen renders. Step 6 is purely informational — the user can safely navigate away from it.

All calls use the **exact same API endpoints and payload formats** the existing dashboard tabs use. No new endpoints or options created.

**CRITICAL: Merge-only updates.** Each API call must spread the full existing option and only override the specific keys the wizard touches. Never remove or overwrite keys the wizard doesn't manage.

```javascript
// 1. Save post types → POST /tta/v1/settings (same as Settings tab)
// Option: tta_settings_data
wizardFetch('settings', {
    ...currentSettings,                                    // preserve all existing keys
    tta__settings_allow_listening_for_post_types: selectedPostTypes,  // only this changes
});

// 2. Save player ID + date range + download perms → POST /tta/v1/customize (same as Customize tab)
// Option: tta_customize_settings
wizardFetch('customize', {
    ...currentCustomize,                                   // preserve all existing keys (colors, borders, etc.)
    buttonSettings: {
        ...currentCustomize.buttonSettings,                // preserve ALL existing buttonSettings keys
        ...(useInProduction && { id: selectedPlayerId }),  // only update id if "Yes, use in production"
        generate_mp3_date_from: dateFrom,
        generate_mp3_date_to: dateTo,
        who_can_download_mp3_file: downloadPermission,
        // DO NOT touch: button_position, display_player_to, colors, size, etc.
    }
});

// 3. Save voice & language → POST /tta/v1/listening (same as Listening tab)
// Option: tta_listening_settings
// Uses FormData format: { fields: JSON.stringify(data), method: "post" }
let listeningData = new FormData();
listeningData.append("fields", JSON.stringify({
    ...currentListening,                                   // preserve ALL existing keys (pitch, rate, volume, elevenlabs_*, etc.)
    tta__listening_lang: selectedLanguage,
    tta__listening_voice: selectedVoice,
    ...(selectedPlayerId == 5 && { tta__listening_voice_model: selectedModel }),
    ...(selectedPlayerId == 6 && { tta__elevenlabs_model: selectedModel }),
}));
listeningData.append("method", "post");
postWithoutImage(apiURL + "tta/v1/listening", listeningData);

// 4. Save analytics → existing analytics save endpoint
// Option: tta_analytics_settings
wizardFetch('save_analytics_settings', {
    ...currentAnalytics,                                   // preserve all existing keys
    tts_enable_analytics: enableAnalytics,
    tts_trackable_post_ids: trackAll ? ['all'] : specificIds,
});

// 5. Save schedule report → POST /tta/v1/save_schedule_report (same as ExportSection)
// Option: tta_schedule_report_settings
wizardFetch('save_schedule_report', {
    ...currentScheduleReport,                              // preserve all existing keys (day, time, include* flags, etc.)
    enabled: digestEnabled,
    frequency: digestFrequency,
    recipients: digestEmail,
});

// 6. Mark Pro onboarding complete
update_option('tta_pro_onboarding_completed', true);
```

**Existing options used (no new ones):**

| Option Name | API Endpoint | Step | Keys Wizard Touches |
|-------------|-------------|------|---------------------|
| `tta_settings_data` | `POST /tta/v1/settings` | Step 1 | `tta__settings_allow_listening_for_post_types` |
| `tta_customize_settings` | `POST /tta/v1/customize` | Step 2, 4 | `buttonSettings.id`, `.generate_mp3_date_from`, `.generate_mp3_date_to`, `.who_can_download_mp3_file` |
| `tta_listening_settings` | `POST /tta/v1/listening` | Step 3 | `tta__listening_lang`, `tta__listening_voice`, `tta__listening_voice_model`, `tta__elevenlabs_model` |
| `tta_analytics_settings` | analytics save endpoint | Step 5 | `tts_enable_analytics`, `tts_trackable_post_ids` |
| `tta_schedule_report_settings` | `POST /tta/v1/save_schedule_report` | Step 5 | `enabled`, `frequency`, `recipients` |

### PHP Changes

**Free plugin — `admin/TTA_Admin.php`:**
- In `enqueue_scripts()`: Add `is_pro_wizard` flag to `ttsWizardData`:
```php
'is_pro_wizard' => TTA_Helper::is_pro_active() && !get_option('tta_pro_onboarding_completed'),
```
- When `is_pro_wizard` is true, `welcome.js` renders a `<div id="pro-wizard-root">` instead of free wizard

**Pro plugin — `TTA_Pro_Admin.php` (or equivalent):**
- Enqueue Pro wizard JS bundle (`pro-wizard.min.js`) when `welcome=1` and Pro is active
- Localize `ttsProWizardData` with:
  - `provider_cards`: Array of provider info (name, ID, voice count, languages, requires_api_key)
  - `current_settings`: Current `tta_settings_data`
  - `current_customize`: Current `tta_customize_settings` (full buttonSettings)
  - `current_listening`: Current `tta_listening_settings` (voice, lang, model, elevenlabs_* etc.)
  - `current_analytics`: Current `tta_analytics_settings`
  - `current_schedule_report`: Current `tta_schedule_report_settings`
  - `admin_email`: `get_option('admin_email')` for email digest default
  - `post_types`: Available post types with published counts
  - `nonce`, `api_url`, `dashboard_url`

**Pro plugin — `TTA_Pro_Activator.php`:**
- On activation: `update_option('tta_pro_onboarding_completed', false, false);`
- Delete `tta_onboarding_completed` to trigger wizard redirect

### Webpack Bundle

The Pro wizard is a **separate bundle** in the Pro plugin's build system:
- Entry: `text-to-audio-pro/src/pro-wizard/index.js`
- Output: `text-to-audio-pro/admin/js/build/pro-wizard.min.js`
- Enqueued only when `welcome=1` and Pro is active
- Mounts to `#pro-wizard-root` div rendered by free plugin's `welcome.js`

---

## Voice Loading Strategy (Per Provider)

| Provider | How Voices Load | Preview Method |
|----------|----------------|----------------|
| AtlasVoice GTTS (3) | No voice list needed (language only) | N/A (generates on server) |
| Google Cloud TTS (4) | Fetch from `tta/v1/voices` → cache localStorage | Google CDN audio URL |
| ChatGPT TTS (5) | Hardcoded 6 voices | OpenAI CDN audio URL |
| ElevenLabs (6) | Fetch from `tta_pro/v1/elevenlabs_voices` → cache localStorage | `preview_url` from API |

**Browser voice comparison:** StepProVoice includes a "Compare with Browser Voice" button that uses `window.speechSynthesis` (same as free wizard) so users can hear the difference.

---

## Edge Cases

1. **User hasn't set up API keys yet:** Skip voice preview, show message "Connect your API key in Integrations to hear a preview." Provider selection still works.
2. **User already completed free wizard:** Pre-populate voice/language from existing settings. Don't reset customization colors.
3. **User clicks "Back" from Step 1:** No back button on Step 1 (it's the first step).
4. **User skips wizard:** Add "Skip Setup" link in header. Sets `tta_pro_onboarding_completed = true` without changing any settings.
5. **Pro deactivated then reactivated:** Check `tta_pro_onboarding_completed` — if already true, don't show wizard again unless reset.

---

## Implementation Order

**Phase A: Free plugin changes (minimal)**
1. **welcome.js** — Add `is_pro_wizard` check, render `<div id="pro-wizard-root">` when Pro wizard is active
2. **TTA_Admin.php** — Add `is_pro_wizard` flag to `ttsWizardData`

**Phase B: Pro plugin — React components**
3. **index.js** — Pro wizard entry point, mounts to `#pro-wizard-root`
4. **ProWelcomeWizard.js** — Container with step navigation (reads existing settings, no extra state)
5. **StepProPostType.js** — Multi-select post type checkboxes
6. **StepProvider.js** — Provider cards (Player 2/3/4/5/6) + "Use in production?" toggle
7. **StepProVoice.js** — Voice/language selection with provider-specific UI + preview
8. **StepPlayerSettings.js** — Date range + download permissions (read/write `tta_customize_settings`)
9. **StepProAnalytics.js** — Analytics toggle + email digest (read/write `tta_schedule_report_settings`)
10. **StepProFinish.js** — Summary + cross-promo
11. **wizardApi.js** — REST API helper

**Phase C: Pro plugin — PHP backend**
12. **TTA_Pro_Admin.php** — Enqueue Pro wizard bundle, localize `ttsProWizardData`
13. **TTA_Pro_Activator.php** — Set Pro onboarding flag on activation
14. **Pro webpack config** — Add `pro-wizard` entry point

**Phase D: Testing**
15. **Browser testing** — Verify all 5 steps + finish, data saving, edge cases
16. **UI/UX review** — Check responsiveness, visual polish, accessibility

---

## Blueprint: Reusable Setup Wizard Pattern for AtlasAiDev Plugins

This section documents the **generic wizard pattern** so the same architecture can be reused for any AtlasAiDev plugin (AI Agent Hub, AR/VR 3D Model, future plugins).

### Core Pattern

```
[PluginSlug]/
  src/dashboard/
    welcome.js                    ← Entry: renders wizard or dashboard
    welcome/
      WelcomeWizard.js            ← Free wizard container
      ProWelcomeWizard.js         ← Pro wizard container (if Pro exists)
      wizardApi.js                ← REST API helper (shared)
      steps/
        Step[Name].js             ← Each step is a self-contained component
```

### Step Component Contract

Every step component follows this interface:

```jsx
const StepExample = ({ data, onChange, wizardData }) => {
    // data: current step's state slice
    // onChange: callback to update parent state
    // wizardData: localized PHP data (post types, settings, etc.)

    return (
        <div>
            <h2>{heading}</h2>
            <p>{description}</p>
            {/* Step-specific form fields */}
        </div>
    );
};
```

### Wizard Container Contract

```jsx
const WizardContainer = () => {
    const [step, setStep] = useState(1);
    const [stepData, setStepData] = useState({/* per-step state */});

    const totalSteps = N;
    const goNext = () => step < totalSteps ? setStep(step + 1) : handleFinish();
    const goBack = () => step > 1 && setStep(step - 1);

    const handleFinish = async () => {
        // 1. Save all settings via REST API
        // 2. Mark onboarding complete
        // 3. Track completion event
        setStep(totalSteps + 1); // Show finish screen
    };

    return (
        <WizardShell step={step} totalSteps={totalSteps} onBack={goBack}>
            {renderStep()}
            <WizardNav onBack={goBack} onNext={goNext} />
        </WizardShell>
    );
};
```

### PHP Backend Contract

```php
// 1. Localize wizard data
wp_localize_script('plugin-wizard', 'wizardData', [
    'post_types'       => $post_types,
    'current_settings' => get_option('plugin_settings', []),
    'is_pro_active'    => Helper::is_pro_active(),
    'nonce'            => wp_create_nonce('wp_rest'),
    'api_url'          => rest_url('plugin/v1/'),
    'dashboard_url'    => admin_url('admin.php?page=plugin-slug'),
    'is_pro_wizard'    => $is_pro && !get_option('plugin_pro_onboarding_completed'),
]);

// 2. REST endpoint saves settings + onboarding flag
// 3. Activation hook resets onboarding flag
// 4. reset_onboard=true URL deletes flag and redirects to welcome=1
```

### Applying to Other Plugins

**AI Agent Hub:**
- Step 1: Choose AI Provider (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Local)
- Step 2: Enter API Key + Test Connection
- Step 3: Enable Abilities (select from 80+)
- Step 4: Configure Workflow (optional first workflow)
- Finish: Summary + cross-promo (Text-to-Speech, AR/VR)

**AR/VR 3D Model:**
- Step 1: Choose Display Mode (AR, VR, 3D Viewer)
- Step 2: Upload First Model or Connect Provider
- Step 3: Product Integration (WooCommerce mapping)
- Step 4: Customize Viewer (colors, controls, placement)
- Finish: Summary + cross-promo (Text-to-Speech, AI Agent Hub)

### Cross-Promo Strategy

Every plugin's Finish step includes a "More from AtlasAiDev" section with cards for sibling plugins. The card data is centralized:

```javascript
const atlasPlugins = {
    'text-to-speech': {
        name: 'Text-to-Speech TTS Accessibility',
        description: 'Add AI-powered audio players to your content',
        url: 'https://wordpress.org/plugins/text-to-audio/',
        icon: '🔊',
    },
    'ai-agent-hub': {
        name: 'AI Workflow Automation — AI Agent Hub',
        description: 'Turn WordPress into an AI-powered hub with 80+ abilities',
        url: 'https://wordpress.org/plugins/ai-workflow-automation-ai-agent-hub/',
        icon: '🤖',
    },
    'ar-vr-3d': {
        name: 'AR/VR 3D Model & Try-On',
        description: 'Add immersive 3D product experiences to your shop',
        url: 'https://wordpress.org/plugins/ar-vr-3d-model-try-on/',
        icon: '🥽',
    },
};
// Each plugin's finish screen shows the OTHER two plugins
```

---

## Design Principles

1. **Simple over complete** — Only ask what's necessary. Advanced settings go in the dashboard.
2. **Show value fast** — Voice preview in Step 3 is the "aha moment." Make it work without API keys if possible.
3. **Pre-populate from free wizard** — Don't re-ask what the user already configured.
4. **Production toggle is key** — Step 2 asks "use in production?" to avoid surprising users by changing their active player.
5. **No extra state** — Wizard reads/writes existing WordPress options directly. No intermediate wizard-specific options.
6. **Skip is always available** — "Skip Setup" link visible on every step.
7. **Mobile-friendly** — Cards stack vertically on narrow screens.
8. **Consistent with free wizard** — Same visual language (card styles, button styles, color scheme).
9. **Lives in Pro plugin** — All wizard code is in `text-to-audio-pro`. Free plugin only provides the mount point.
10. **Cross-promo is subtle** — Only on Finish screen, presented as "More from AtlasAiDev" not as ads.
